      "id": "xu-zhimo-poems-s0010-p00010",
      "source_en": "\"Don't squeeze me, 痛,\" you said, with your brows gently tightened, that \"痛,\" a perfectly round half-breath that rolled and turned on the tip of the tongue. A pair of eyes also spoke, and in their light rose the secret of the heart-spring. Dream scattered across the net of gauzy silk. \"Where are you?\" \"Let us die,\" you said.",
